<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Landin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1250</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Landin was concluded in 1250 between Barnim I, duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a>, and the margraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, John I and Otto III. By it Barnim ceded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uckermark">Uckermark</a>, a region north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> long contested between the two powers, to Brandenburg. It marked the steady advance of Brandenburg at Pomerania's expense in the thirteenth century.</p></div>
